    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Temperament:</strong> Peaceful. Can be kept in pairs or a group.</li><li><strong>Max size:</strong> 5 inches (about 12.5 cm)</li><li><strong>TDS:</strong> 60–200</li><li><strong>pH:</strong> 6.5–7</li><li><strong>Temperature:</strong> 75–82 °F (24–28 °C)</li><li><strong>Diet:</strong> Carnivorous</li><li><strong>Breeding:</strong> Mouthbrooder</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>TDS 60–200. Kept in soft water with low TDS, but they are more tolerant of water conditions.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Can be fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Males are generally larger with longer fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>The only one in its group, the Betta anabatoides complex. Also known as the Giant Betta as this species can get up to 5 inches in length. Another mouthbrooder type betta originating from South Kalimantan in Indonesia. These can be maintained in a pair or a group. Males are generally larger with longer fins. This betta appears to be very peaceful and can be kept in groups.</p>"
    }
